94e3e73b65e1be5d9667e6998d1ac98f7209d0df99b01","event_uuid":"f57465d4-41d3-422a-9962-f137cfcd623e","position":{"commit_sha":"e5c619d7ada2080d39b533f14fb37822f7225d0a","position":"1786757129580894001-f57465d4-41d3-422a-9962-f137cfcd623e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0ff0a8c1d25067b44f929ce74278b7e8be15c0018fe205414dae4c606fa25332","event_uuid":"c1908438-2ae2-4522-9677-bff0796643ae","position":{"commit_sha":"0935a944621b03a55dc90682970e943ec1ef8230","position":"1786757291040997001-c1908438-2ae2-4522-9677-bff0796643ae"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786757095098457001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"058aa77d-012d-4780-b990-d2870c9f048a","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"41d2-2814-a368-4c79"},{"link_uuid":"f57465d4-41d3-422a-9962-f137cfcd623e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"325e-7e85-d0d6-4318"},{"link_uuid":"02776352-26bb-4615-ba17-7935d7788255","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9d44-c0c0-8d4d-4074"}],"description":"## Context\n\nTwo consecutive successful macOS Gerrit Verify jobs after change 1730 still report tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py::test_benchmark_commit_count_is_ceil_per_pass at 21.05s and 29.38s. Closed ticket curricular-mean-cuckoo already removed the dominant redundant work and explicitly locks this contract at 3,000 tickets, 3,000 comments, 24 crash-safe import commits, and >=10x commit reduction. This follow-up must preserve that exact behavioral/performance-scale contract and remove only proven redundant work.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. Reproduce the exact N=3000 node on current origin/main with repeated wall-time samples and a full call-count/cumulative-time profile. Separate test construction, importer composition, validation, filesystem writes, Git index/commit subprocesses, materialization, and cleanup.\n2. Form competing hypotheses from the profile and run one controlled experiment per hypothesis. Compare against the already-landed author-cache and stale-sweep optimization; do not infer from aggregate suite time.\n3. Cross-check the ticket store for prior decisions and compare the proven mechanism with popular maintained OSS bulk-import/test patterns before proposing a change. The curricular-mean-cuckoo workload and durability constraints remain controlling.\n4. If the remaining cost is redundant setup or production-path work, add a deterministic held-out oracle for the exact call/effect count, prove RED, implement the narrow optimization, and prove GREEN plus exact-defect mutation RED. If the remaining time is irreducible work needed for the locked scale contract, report that result and evaluate scheduling/tier placement without removing the test from macOS unless equivalent platform assurance is proven.\n5. Verify the unchanged N=3000/6000-event/24-commit assertions, import idempotency, rollback, crash-resume, clean-index, author and stale-sweep lifecycle, focused unit/interface suites, lint, typecheck, and the full Gerrit Verify matrix. Report before/after macOS runner-seconds and overall critical-path effect.\n\n## Test contract card\n\nauthoritative_contract: curricular-mean-cuckoo and tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py preserve N=3000, 6,000 events, exactly 24 crash-safe import commits, >=10x commit reduction, complete state, rollback, and resume.\ntrigger_preconditions: fresh real Git-backed store importing the fixed synthetic corpus through public rebar.import_tickets.\nproduction_path: rebar.import_tickets through import composition, batch staging/commit, and materialization.\ntest_tier: real-Git integration on every supported CI platform currently executing this node.\nobservable_postcondition: identical ticket/comment state, event attribution, commit graph/count, clean index, and deterministic collaborator/effect counts with lower measured wall time.\nnegative_control: independent interactive writes, failure rollback, later-chunk resume, and existing-ticket imports retain current semantics.\ncollateral_invariants: no test, platform cell, mutation shard, coverage measurement, event validation, durability boundary, or contractual assertion is removed or weakened.\nci_gate: focused repeated benchmark evidence plus full Gerrit Verified gate.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Current macOS time over 20s is reproduced and individually attributed to concrete operations with call counts and cumulative time.\n- [ ] The exact N=3000, 6,000-event, 24-commit, >=10x, complete-state, rollback, and crash-resume contracts remain unchanged and green.\n- [ ] Any implementation is guarded by a held-out deterministic oracle, exact-defect mutation evidence, and negative controls for interactive/failure behavior.\n- [ ] Ticket-store prior decisions and relevant maintained OSS practice are documented before remediation.\n- [ ] Repeated same-host before/after results quantify test and runner-time savings; time remains evidence, not a flaky threshold.\n- [ ] Focused suites, lint, typecheck, full Gerrit Verify, LLM-Review, and merge are green before closure.","env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py","reason":"retain and strengthen the exact N=3000 integration oracle while profiling its remaining long pole"},{"path":"src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py","reason":"likely import orchestration seam; change only if profiling proves redundant work"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/event_append.py","reason":"likely bounded batch orchestration seam; change only if profiling proves redundant work"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/event_prepare.py","reason":"likely event preparation seam; change only if profiling proves redundant work"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/staging.py","reason":"likely real-Git staging seam; change only if profiling proves redundant work"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","managed_refs":[["relates_to","325e-7e85-d0d6-4318"],["relates_to","9d44-c0c0-8d4d-4074"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"bf4cc775-3a9e-4199-b733-3623c1056f3b","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["ci","performance","tests","import"],"ticket_id":"c5be-ce38-60a6-47ea","ticket_type":"task","title":"Eliminate remaining macOS N=3000 import benchmark long pole","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["275f0725-4c87-4ee0-abb1-580bdfd2247c","e1071b3a-b368-4916-9017-0530819a5415","058aa77d-012d-4780-b990-d2870c9f048a","f57465d4-41d3-422a-9962-f137cfcd623e","c1908438-2ae2-4522-9677-bff0796643ae","bf4cc775-3a9e-4199-b733-3623c1056f3b","02776352-26bb-4615-ba17-7935d7788255"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786772519401666001,"uuid":"7793129a-74f3-4512-bf92-cc350c666693"}